      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While I like the lay explanations they put in the documentation as a start, I also really wish they would write the properties in actual physics terms somewhere. They list, for advanced, the properties: Pull, Momentum, and stiffness. My mind assumes spring constant, mass, and damping. But the wording implies something different and also they don't behave that way.\nIf they are instead using damped frequency and undamped frequency or damping ratio it would be nice to have a more advanced explanation.\nAlso stiffness is still really confusing as its wording. Stiffness and Pull have the same meaning, they are both written how i would write the description of a spring/spring force.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-26T15:04:10.279Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While the basic the parameters are briefly explained in the documentation people still have trouble wrapping their head on how to actually configure everything. It would be nice to have some better visuals (e.g. a chart such as this https://twitter.com/NaraWithVR/status/1518717396684619777) in the documentation that show how a setting affects the physic simulation. Maybe even a few videos/GIFs showcasing when a certain setting should be used like done in angle limits section. Yes, people can experiment with it themselves, but it does not make it more accessible.\nP.s. it would be nice if mathematics behind it, or at least how the forces interact with each other is also published <3",
